Myth-Direction

2026-11-12

Well, I have some time away from work and I might actually get some time to work on my personal projects outside of housework, volunteering duties, and crap my wife wants to do. Sorry if that seems a bit down, I'm just mentally and physically exhausted at the moment. Sleeping like crap isn't helping. I'm stuck in a funk at the moment and the crawl out of it is happening very slowly. But, there's shiny stuff along the way! 

Trying to figure out exactly where I want to go with some of the projects. They're mostly working with RPGs and fiction/settings. I have a sort of ADHD that causes me to hop between genres and likes whenever the real work gets to the metaphorical workbench. I'll sort it all out though. That's what we do, dig in and make it work. 

I think I might 'retheme' my Gemini capsule to more closely follow the setting of the Paranoia tabletop RPG. That has been one of my all time favorite fictional settings for a very long time. I was going to go more with an undead pirate crew sort of thing, which is also a long time writing interest, but my brain seems to constantly default back to Alpha Complex (or at least my favorite homebrewed sectors within) frequently. And it's a fun theme to work with.

I probably shouldn't do much writing when I'm sleep deprived and frustrated. It'd be easier not to if I knew why I was frustrated and if it were not a long term issue. 

Perhaps I'll come back later. 